@id=still-to-come-is-marked-where-it-is-written @kind=decision
Feature: What is still to come is marked where it is written, and what is built is live and stays so

  Not a folder that decides what is built, nor a change kept in a file of its own until it is merged
  into its feature: a feature or a rule still to come declares a maturity where it is written, for a
  rule is the unit that is built and only a tag can mark one, and what declares none is live, a test
  that `sdp check` holds to the git base. A feature wholly still to come also sits in its area's
  backlog folder, which repeats its maturity for whoever browses the area. The price is a fact written twice, a feature file that mixes live rules and rules
  still to come told apart only by their tags, a replacement before anything live can be removed,
  and a guarantee that holds only where git has a base to compare with.
